<title>UK: Wickes names new chief executive - paper.</title>
<headline>Wickes names new chief executive - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wickes Plc, the do-it-yourself retailer rocked by accounting irregularities, said it had appointed Bill Grimsey as its chief executive, the Daily Telegraph newspaper said.</p>
<p>Grimsey has been managing director of Wickes Building Supplies, the company's main trading subsidiary, since July, the paper said.</p>
<p>Former senior managers of Wickes are under investigation by the Serious Fraud Office, Britain's top fraud watchdog.</p>
